    <cqft-part-title|Renormalisation: why two of them>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture<nbsp>5>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Scales and power counting>

    \;

    <\equation*>
      g<rsub|q>=\<gamma\>*q<rsup|-1/2><around|(|<text|dimensionless
      coupling>|)>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      r<rsub|q>=<around|(|q/\<gamma\>|)><rsup|1/2><around|(|\<gamma\>*r<rsub|q><rsup|2>=q:<text|nonlinearity>\<approx\><text|regulator>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Free field at resolution <math|q>: <math|<math-up|Var>X<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|1/2>>,
    typical size <math|q<rsup|1/4>=g<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|q>\<ll\>r<rsub|q>>.

    Rooted norm of a vertex <math|T<around|(|x<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,x<rsub|k>|)>>
    and field ball:

    <\equation*>
      s<around|(|T|)>=max<rsub|i> sup<rsub|x<rsub|i>>
      <big|int><around|\||T|\|>*<big|prod><rsub|j\<ne\>i>\<mathd\>x<rsub|j>,<space|2em><math-ss|S><rsub|k><around|(|g|)>=sup<rsub|\<cal-B\><rsub|q>> s*<around|(|D<rsup|k-1>*g|)>,<space|2em>\<cal-B\><rsub|q>=<around|{|<around|\<\|\|\>|y|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<less\>2*r<rsub|q>|}>.
    </equation*>

    Natural size of the <math|k>th vertex of the <strong|loop corrections>:

    <\equation*>
      <math-ss|S><rsub|k>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q>*<space|0.17em>q*<space|0.17em>r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>*<space|2em><around|(|k=4:\<gamma\>*g<rsub|q>|)>.
    </equation*>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The loop estimate>

    \;

    \;

    \;

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Loop estimate>

      A closed loop with <math|p> vertices:
      <math|s<around|(|<text|loop>|)>\<leqslant\>C*a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>*<space|0.17em>q<rsup|-<around|(|p-1|)>>*<big|prod><rsub|i>s<around|(|T<rsub|i>|)>>
      (two propagators in <math|L<rsup|2>>, the others in operator norm).
      After the <math|q> integration a one-loop term is of size
      <math|g<rsub|q>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>; every further loop gains a
      factor <math|g<rsub|q>>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The seed and the corrections>

    \;

    <strong|Seed> (one loop): replace <math|D\<cal-F\>> by <math|\<gamma\>
    y<rsup|2>> and integrate from <math|q=\<infty\>>, with the linear part
    subtracted,

    <\equation*>
      \<ell\><rsub|q><around|(|y|)><around|(|x|)>=\<gamma\>
      y<around|(|x|)><around|[|G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><around|(|x,x|)>-C<rsub|q><around|(|x,x|)>|]>,<space|1em>
      G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+\<gamma\>
      y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>.
    </equation*>

    Leading term = bubble, <math|s<around|(|D<rsup|3>\<ell\><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>|)>=6\<gamma\><rsup|2>a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>>.

    <strong|Corrections.> <math|\<Pi\>> removes the linear jet,
    <math|M<rsub|q>=\<mu\><rsub|q>+\<Theta\><rsub|q>> a linear path,
    <math|U'=\<lambda\> y<rsup|3>>,

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]>=-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsup|2>>D<rsup|2><around|(|U'+\<ell\>|)>,<space|1em>
      R=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>+D<around|(|U'+\<ell\>|)>|)><rsup|-1>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      \<ell\><rsup|<around|[|0|]>>=\<ell\>,<space|1em>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>><rsub|q>=\<ell\><rsub|q>-<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\><around|(|\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>|]>-\<partial\><rsub|s>\<ell\><rsub|s>|)><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>
      s,<space|1em> j=0,1,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|o><rsub|q>=U'+M<rsub|q>y+\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q><space|1em><text|on
      the ball.>
    </equation*>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Where the iteration comes from>

    Force equation for <math|\<cal-F\><rsub|q>=U'+M<rsub|q>y+\<ell\><rsub|q>>,
    <math|\<Pi\>\<ell\><rsub|q>=\<ell\><rsub|q>>:

    <\equation*>
      <around|(|\<partial\><rsub|q>M<rsub|q>|)>y+\<partial\><rsub|q>\<ell\><rsub|q>=\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsub|q>|]><around|(|y|)>.
    </equation*>

    <math|\<Pi\>> and <math|1-\<Pi\>> split it:

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|nonlinear part>, integrable at <math|q=\<infty\>>
      (<math|k\<geqslant\>4> legs), with <math|\<ell\><rsub|\<infty\>>=0>:
      a fixed point,
      <math|\<ell\><rsub|q>=-<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\>\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsub|s>|]><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>s>;
      approximated by <strong|Picard steps>, the seed being the first;

      <item><strong|linear part>, divergent (tadpole, sunset): solved
      exactly by the mass equation; gives the counterterm.
    </itemize>

    <\myframed>
      Each step gains one loop, one <math|g<rsub|q>>. The defect of
      <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|o>> is the loop difference of the last two steps:

      <\equation*>
        \<partial\><rsub|q>\<cal-F\><rsup|o><rsub|q>-\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]>=\<Pi\><around*|(|\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|]>-\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]>|)>=O<around|(|g<rsub|q><rsup|3>|)>.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Seed and corrections in graphs>

    \;

