    <small|<with|color|dark grey|Each step inserts the previous correction
    into the loop: one more loop, one more <math|g<rsub|q>>. Two steps give a
    defect of order <math|g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>.>>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The mass>

    \;

    The linear jet is not iterated: it is solved exactly by <math|M>,

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>M<rsub|q>=-\<gamma\><math-up|Tr><around|(|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>|)>I-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>>D<rsup|3>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>,<space|1em>
      R<rsub|0,q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>,
    </equation*>

    with <math|\<mu\><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>=b>,
    <math|<around|\||b|\|>\<leqslant\> B\<gamma\> q<rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/2>>,
    at an <strong|auxiliary scale> <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>, and
    <math|\<Theta\><rsub|q>\<to\>0> as <math|q\<to\>\<infty\>>. Bare mass
    <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>=<math-up|lim><rsub|q\<to\>\<infty\>>\<mu\><rsub|q>>:
    an output of the flow.

    <strong|For> <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>> <strong|large, uniformly in>
    <math|N><strong|.> Unique solution in a ball,
    <math|<around|\||\<mu\><rsub|q>|\|>\<leqslant\> C\<gamma\> q<rsup|1/2>>,
    <math|v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\>
    C\<gamma\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>>; increments
    <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k><around|(|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>-\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j-1|]>>|)>\<leqslant\>
    C<rsub|k>g<rsub|q><rsup|j+1>q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>; and the defect of
    <math|\<cal-F\><rsup|<math-up|o>>>: <math|S<rsub|4><around|(|\<cal-D\><rsup|<math-up|o>><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\>
    C\<gamma\><rsup|5>q<rsup|-3>>.

    <strong|Explicit counterterm.> <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>=r-3\<lambda\><math-up|Tr>
    C+6\<lambda\><rsup|2><big|int> C<rsup|3>> is admissible: the measure does
    not depend on <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Two mass renormalisations>

    \;

    The two divergent self-energies of Appendix<nbsp>A.2 of Lecture<nbsp>4:

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Tadpole>: <math|-\<gamma\>*<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|\<infty\>><math-up|Tr>R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q\<approx\>-3*\<lambda\><math-up|Tr>C\<sim\>-N>.
      Wick ordering: <math|<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*\<varphi\><rsup|4>-<frac|3|2>*\<lambda\>*c*\<varphi\><rsup|2>=<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*H<rsub|4>*<around|(|\<varphi\>;c|)>+>const.

      <item><strong|Sunset>: contracting the bubble in
      <math|D<rsup|3>\<ell\><around|(|0|)>> with <math|R<rsub|0><rsup|2>> and
      integrating gives the two-loop self-energy,

      <\equation*>
        6*\<lambda\><rsup|2>*<big|int>C<rsup|3>\<approx\><frac|3*\<lambda\><rsup|2>|8*\<pi\><rsup|2>>*log
        N<space|1em><around|(|=2*\<gamma\><rsub|T>*<text|of Lecture 4, with
        >\<lambda\><rsub|<with|math-font-family|rm|L4>>=\<lambda\>/4|)>.
      </equation*>
    </itemize>

    Power counting: nothing else. In the flow: the integrals from
    <math|q=\<infty\>> of all vertices with <math|k\<geqslant\>4> legs
    converge; only the linear jet needs a boundary condition.

    <math|\<mu\><rsub|q>> at fixed <math|q> has a limit as
    <math|N\<to\>\<infty\>>; <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>> does not. <strong|Never
    interchange the two limits.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The two mass renormalisations in graphs>

    \;

